---
description: When to comment, and the 60-character comment format.
alwaysApply: true
---

# General
- Do not comment what the next line already says.
  That includes a `CreateDefaultSubobject` name and
  "NetCore is already listed in JoA_Arena.Build.cs."
- A comment states what the code cannot show: a
  gameplay rule, a replication choice, an engine
  trap, or a constraint. Say what breaks without it.
- No comment line exceeds 60 characters.

# Form
- At most 60 characters total: `// Comment text`
- Longer than 60, on a method, an enum item, or
  logic:
  /* Line 1 text.
   * Line 2 text. */
- A class, struct, interface, or other type uses a
  doc comment, any length:
  /**
   * Definition description.
   */
- Do not use a doc comment on a method, a function,
  or an enum item.
